  "summary": "A traditional Mexican pottery style characterized by its distinctive black, unglazed finish.",
  "description": "Features smooth, matte black surfaces with simple, elegant forms and occasional engraved or incised decorations. Created from a specific local clay that turns black during firing without oxygen, this technique has been used in the Oaxaca region since pre-Columbian times and was notably refined by Doña Rosa in the 1950s.",
